{"id":"ab7bcc93-3656-46a2-972f-b3ea090526df","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"5e7cf04016024fe5","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/node-modules-provider.ts","baseline":{"blob":"920c9a38089bd55e708c8eec781c89c194995911","start":4466,"end":4565},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","deployBase","=","location",".","pathname",".","slice","(","0",",","location",".","pathname",".","indexOf","(","\"","/__vscode__/","\"",")","+","1",")","||","\"","/","\""]},"context":{"before":"e20d9b8c25f8f9e7","after":"c441978da20f311a"}},"payload":{"text":"The deploy base (\"/editor/\" on GitHub Pages, \"/\" locally): this provider runs in the workbench iframe at\n<base>/__vscode__/host.html, and the service worker is scoped to <base>, so requests must sit under <base>\nto be intercepted (the SW matches /workspace/ under any prefix — see coi-serviceworker.js). A root-absolute\n/workspace/… URL would escape the SW scope on a subpath deploy.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:52:15.816Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:52:15.816Z"}
{"id":"b8da786c-2a09-40af-a0f0-aa98937873b1","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"c3b1970de08cad4c","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/node-modules-provider.ts","baseline":{"blob":"83203b03d5a987571bf71fbd0f3c20b56086151f","start":6957,"end":7044},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","real","=","aliases","[","pkg","]","===","undefined","?","\"","","\"",":","`","&p=","${","encodeURIComponent","(","aliases","[","pkg","]",")","}","","`"]},"context":{"before":"64c9c091d8b44899","after":"d4ebddccffbc0dfd"}},"payload":{"text":"(an npm alias is fetched as the package it is: `p`, which the fallback asks the CDN for instead of the folder's name)","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:52:00.147Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:52:00.147Z"}
{"id":"c586e48d-781b-46d3-aa71-08acf5ed2217","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"485bb3908b5bd9f4","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/node-modules-provider.ts","baseline":{"blob":"8e0502f2ee9a09f78a8a1142925375e08d8a3f0a","start":3868,"end":3913},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","log","=","logger","(","{","\"","source","\"",":","\"","workbench","\"","}",")"]},"context":{"before":"00b01fad035dd5ba","after":"c4a96ff4940e8879"}},"payload":{"text":"Each prefetch is a span: it crosses the network, and what asked for it waits on it.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:52:23.491Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:52:23.491Z"}
{"id":"dcee08fd-95f1-47b3-b407-c5bd40387dc0","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"4b5a656074b851d8","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/node-modules-provider.ts","baseline":{"blob":"9c58ffb5e373a77beeafe5122076ed40ddf235b7","start":3552,"end":3576},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","PREFETCH_DEPTH","=","3"]},"context":{"before":"f070f66f63c14973","after":"00b01fad035dd5ba"}},"payload":{"text":"How deep `prefetchFor` follows a config's relative imports: a config and the few files of its own it imports.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:52:31.296Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:52:31.296Z"}
{"id":"df14e709-ae5d-4d25-a771-241d2b6b51b8","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"9217a8849e220495","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/node-modules-provider.ts","baseline":{"blob":"8c93b5563d1429e5d4e7045fe8c9907dc9f61940","start":17429,"end":17789},"shape":{"type":"For","atoms":["for","(","const","method","of","[","\"","stat","\"",",","\"","readFile","\"",",","\"","readdir","\"","]","as","const",")","{","const","original","=","provider","[","method","]",".","bind","(","provider",")","as","(","resource",":","{","\"","path","\"",":","string","}",")","=>","unknown",";","(","provider","as","unknown","as","Record","<","string",",","unknown",">",")","[","method","]","=","(","resource",":","{","\"","path","\"",":","string","}",")",":","unknown","=>","timeCall","(","\"","node_modules","\"",",","method",",","vscodeCaller","(",")",",","resource",".","path",",","(",")","=>","original","(","resource",")",")",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"23b20fc1201c257e","after":"8f4b4447a0200983"}},"payload":{"text":"(each read counted at the boundary: VS Code's file service into node_modules, by operation, with its path —\nfs-boundaries.ts, the metrics plane's `fs` — by who in VS Code asked, fs-caller.ts's vscodeCaller)","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:51:12.619Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:51:12.619Z"}
{"id":"e9385b98-8173-4195-a4f1-3785f759d3e1","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"78c677969381d5a0","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/node-modules-provider.ts","baseline":{"blob":"69bdafd74a8d08fae229562c88210c97b2691f9d","start":6353,"end":6386},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","{","pkg","}","=","splitPackage","(","rel",")"]},"context":{"before":"756db9ca834079b3","after":"64c9c091d8b44899"}},"payload":{"text":"Fetch the REAL same-origin node_modules path. A store miss there is answered by the resolver's CDN\nfallback — the SW (prod) or build/package-types.ts nodeModulesCdnPlugin (dev) fetches the package from the CDN and\nhands it back same-origin (the fold-in that retired `__proxy__`; see coi-serviceworker.js). The\npinned version rides along as `?v=` so the served source matches the type-checker snapshot's version;\n`?meta` asks for the directory listing. `served()` above guarantees the version is defined here.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:52:04.064Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:52:04.064Z"}
{"id":"ef04e04e-140d-4e92-b243-122429d2af3c","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"2f85c8d453c9cdb1#0","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/node-modules-provider.ts","baseline":{"blob":"d81741ad6aab803ced4ebb83456ef9740235f09e","start":14880,"end":15073},"shape":{"type":"If","atoms":["if","(","!","fileResults",".","has","(","rel",")",")","{","ensureFile","(","rel",",","resource",")",";","return","Promise",".","reject","(","notFound","(",")",")",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"fbd630f87e564364#0","after":"7e0116d5b150f82e"}},"payload":{"text":"Existence via the ACTUAL FILE (404-aware), NOT `?meta`. unpkg's `?meta` lies: it returns\n`200 {files:[]}` for ANY path — existent or not — so a `?meta`-based stat reported every probe as a\nreal 0-byte file, and readFile then 404'd, so tsserver resolved the import to a dead file (\"is not a\nmodule\") and shadowed @types. The actual file 404s correctly, so mirror readFile here.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:51:21.256Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:51:21.256Z"}
{"id":"faa26e27-add6-470e-afb9-9fc8e707fcf2","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"5379ed49c2e054ef","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/node-modules-provider.ts","baseline":{"blob":"fb27d9a55668086abc6d1d0da933b9e5ce0e4ffe","start":8032,"end":8092},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","metaResults","=","new","Map","<","string",",","UnpkgMeta","|","undefined",">","(",")"]},"context":{"before":"6dae0d828a2baaa1","after":"d46ada32c7e92ba2"}},"payload":{"text":"SYNCHRONOUS result caches. stat/readFile/readdir must answer the TS type-checker WITHOUT awaiting the\nnetwork: that checker reads through the @vscode/sync-api SAB bridge, which blocks a worker thread on the\nreply, so an `await fetch(...)` here DEADLOCKS first-load analysis — workspace-fs throws notFound for a\nnot-yet-acquired type, the checker falls through to this overlay, and hangs forever (\"Analyzing…\"). Instead\nserve resolved results synchronously and, on a miss, FAIL FAST (notFound) while fetching in the background;\nthe fetch caches the result and fires a change event (announce), so the checker re-reads and resolves. The\noverlay was always \"eventually-consistent\" — this just stops it blocking the synchronous reader. (Async\ngo-to-definition uses the same methods; a first read may notFound and resolve on the follow-up change.)","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:51:56.253Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:51:56.253Z"}
